==============================================================================
G1. THE LOSS STRATUM, AND WHAT ITS DATA CAN SUPPORT
==============================================================================
  peterson description     4146 trials over  251 distinct problems
  peterson experience     16584 trials over  239 distinct gambles
  ** the experience arm adds trials on the SAME gambles, so it
     cannot raise the effective sample for a coordinate term **

  q slope on pure-loss gambles   -0.3609
  problem-clustered bootstrap    sd 0.0698   95% CI [-0.5034, -0.2368]
  contains zero: NO

  DETECTION LIMIT. with 251 problems the clustered sd is 0.070, so a
  two-sided test at the conventional level can only detect a slope
  of about 0.20 or larger. The gain-side slope is +0.34.
  ** the mirror-image slope could be anything from zero to the size
     of the gain-side slope and this corpus could not tell **

==============================================================================
G2. THE FREE SURFACE, FINER, AND CALIBRATED AGAINST CELL NOISE
==============================================================================
  mixed gambles 55985 trials over 3314 problems

    grid   cells   weighted R^2   max resid
     5x5      23          0.307       10.19
     6x6      33          0.338       10.36
     8x8      48          0.334        8.91
    10x10     75          0.272        8.23

  CALIBRATION. simulate from the FITTED QUADRATIC, re-estimate the
  free surface, and project. If the quadratic were true this is the
  R^2 it would score, and the deficit is cell noise rather than
  missing structure.

    observed R^2 at 5x5                 0.307
    R^2 if the quadratic were TRUE      0.930  (mean of 12 simulations,
                                              sd 0.021)
    deficit attributable to real missing structure   0.623

    ** the quadratic misses real structure, not just noise **

